# Cell function map for NangateOpenCellLibrary_PDKv1_2_v2008_10.
#
# read_cell_func_map stamps a function and a type onto the cells in PLDB, so a
# LEF-only flow can tell combinational cells from sequential ones without
# parsing Liberty. read_lib sets the same thing, but this library's liberty is
# 27 MB and reading it to learn that DFF_X2 is a flop is a poor trade.
#
# It matters to hier_place. The anchor hypergraph keeps the blocks, the ports
# and the sequential cells as anchors and collapses each cone of combinational
# logic between them into one hyperedge. A flop the tool cannot type is not an
# anchor, so it gets collapsed away with the logic around it and the placement
# loses the very nodes whose position it should be deciding.
#
#   <cell>  <type>  [function]     cell may glob with * and ?
#                                  the first line that matches a cell wins
#
# Order matters, so the catch-all is last. Every family here is a real macro
# in that LEF, taken from its MACRO lines rather than assumed.

# Flops, both plain and scan, with every reset/set variant
DFF_*       seq     flop
DFFR_*      seq     flop
DFFS_*      seq     flop
DFFRS_*     seq     flop
SDFF_*      seq     flop
SDFFR_*     seq     flop
SDFFS_*     seq     flop
SDFFRS_*    seq     flop

# Latches. DLH is active high, DLL active low, TLAT is the transparent latch
DLH_*       seq     latch
DLL_*       seq     latch
TLAT_*      seq     latch

# Clock cells. A gate holds state, the buffer does not
CLKGATETST_* seq    clockgate
CLKGATE_*   seq     clockgate
CLKBUF_*    comb    buffer

# Physical-only cells: no logic, but they are not sequential either
FILLCELL_*  comb    fill
ANTENNA_*   comb    antenna
LOGIC0_*    comb    tielow
LOGIC1_*    comb    tiehigh

# Everything else in this library is combinational: the gates, the adders
# (FA, HA), the muxes, and the tristates
*           comb
